    "explanation": "To the rider and the driver: this dispute concerns trip TRP-02860, a RYDE_POOL (pooled) ride, and the rider's contested amount of SGD 1.50 out of the SGD 23.51 charged. The claim does not succeed, and the present payment state stands.\n\nThe baseline the rider used is the wrong one. On a pooled trip, POL-RD-12 measures excess against the matched-itinerary optimal on the trip record, which is trip_record.optimal_distance_km = 16.0 km — not the solo-rider figure of 11.5 km, which is carried as trip_record.solo_optimal_distance_km for reference only. The trip record's optimal_route_source confirms the matched pooled itinerary with one co-rider, and the driver's statement says the same. Distance spent collecting the co-rider on a platform-matched pooled itinerary is part of that itinerary and is excluded from excess under POL-RD-12.\n\nOn the governing distance figure — gps_trace.trace_distance_km = 16.96 km, which governs over the rounded trip_record.actual_distance_km of 17.0 km under POL-RD-01 — the excess over 16.0 km is 0.96 km, or 6.00%. POL-RD-01 requires the excess to exceed BOTH 20% of the optimal distance (3.20 km) and 0.8 km in absolute terms. The absolute limb passes (0.96 km) but the percentage limb fails (6.00% against 20%), so no route deviation is established and the derived deviation block records status 'no deviation'. The GPS trace is complete and unimpaired for policy purposes (133 fixes at a 10-second sample interval, 100.0% coverage, zero gaps, maximum gap 0.0 s), so POL-RD-07(a)–(c) are not met, no corroboration requirement arises, and the trace is relied on directly.\n\nBecause no deviation is established, POL-RD-02 does not run and no distance-or-time refund is available to the rider; the fare model is METERED, so POL-RD-11 does not apply either. For transparency only, the fare ledger derives a recomputed fare of SGD 22.76 against the SGD 23.51 charged, but that figure is not payable and the rider's SGD 1.50 has no line of the fare breakdown behind it. No billing-integrity correction is due under POL-RD-09(4): the fare breakdown carries zero ERP lines, zero tolls and a zero airport surcharge, and the trip neither originates nor ends at an airport.\n\nOn the driver's side: no repeat-deviation pattern is established under POL-RD-06 (driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d is 0 against 185 completed trips in 90 days), so that clause is not engaged and no driver-conduct referral is made. The driver's profile is used only for the test POL-RD-06 names and for nothing else, and the lifetime prior_deviation_flags counter is not that test. The chat log is empty (0 messages), so no rider-requested detour under POL-RD-04 arises and none is needed. The rider's profile (deviation_claims_60d 0, deviation_claims_60d_substantiated 0) is used only to confirm the POL-RD-08 corroboration trigger is not in play; it neither supports nor defeats the claim.\n\nThe bundle contains no traffic advisory for this corridor (EV-ADVIS-02860-01 is MISSING at weight 0.0). No party needed one and none was invoked: the claim fails the POL-RD-01 threshold before any exculpatory clause is reached, so the absent advisory neither helps nor hurts the driver and triggers no escalation under POL-RD-10(5).\n\nOutcome: NO_ACTION. The charge of SGD 23.51 remains in place and no refund is issued, and no driver compensation is payable. Confidence is 0.95: the deciding facts — the matched-itinerary optimal of 16.0 km and the trace distance of 16.96 km — are carried by EV-TRIP-02860 and EV-GPS-02860, both at weight_multiplier 1.0, so the POL-GEN-02(2) cap is 1.0. The monetary effect is nil, below the execution threshold. This ruling was made without human review; either party may appeal it once within 30 days under POL-GEN-04."
